2026-11-21 04:16 Review (unreagent-reviewer, 2026-11-21): CHANGES NEEDED (README only; code approved). Files: cmd/launcher/hermes.go (parseYAMLFile, emptyDocument), cmd/launcher/hermes_test.go, README.md (hermes-setup) in worktree-agent-aa1f2e2fa22aeac6a, base 8f24738. The check is the same green run as on k116 (gofmt -l, go vet linux+windows, go test -count=1 ./..., -race -count=3 ./cmd/launcher, make linux, make windows, go mod verify). Mutations: counting a bare '---' as a document fails TestHermesSetupAcceptsEmptyTrailingDocument (5 cases) and one refusal case; removing the multi-document check fails all 6 refusal cases plus the local.yaml test. The code is fail-safe: every refused input holds a comment that yaml.v3 hangs on the second document, which the rewrite would drop.
